            "ImageDescription": {
              "value": "<i>Landgirl's Day- Everyday Life and Agriculture in West Sussex, England, UK, 1944</i><br>\n29 year old Land Girl Rosalind Cox stands on the back of a truck and uses a 9 inch hook to pass hay bales down from the truck to the waiting hands of a farm hand below.  The bales, according to the original caption, weigh 80 pounds.  The bales are pulled down the plank of wood acting as a ramp, and are stacked by the farmhand.  They are working on Mr Tupper's farm, Bignor, West Sussex.",
              "source": "commons-desc-page"
            },
